@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide footbox
actor Student
boundary UI
control Reservation
control Core
title S2 - Pickup (Core API v1.1, D-015/D-017)
Student -> UI: Confirm pickup at origin
UI -> Reservation: Reservation ID, origin, vehicle version
Reservation -> Reservation: Validate actor; read owned Reservation / Trip first
alt Existing matching Trip
  Reservation --> UI: Same Trip ID and recorded pickup / due time
else New pickup
  Reservation -> Core: Enter core.unit_of_work()
  group One repository transaction under Core lock
    Reservation -> Reservation: Reread booking / Trip; check owner and origin
    Reservation -> Core: get_config().as_of; get_vehicle()
    Core --> Reservation: Authoritative time and vehicle state/version
    alt Confirmed and now < expiry, eligible own Reserved vehicle
      Reservation -> Core: transition_vehicle(PICKUP, version, claim_id)
      Core -> Core: Validate own vehicle claim; free source space\nVehicle InUse; clear Hub / space
      Core --> Reservation: Vehicle result or Err
      Reservation -> Core: release_claim(booking.claim_id, actor)
      Reservation -> Reservation: Add unique Trip; due = now + planned duration\nUpdate Reservation to Active via uow.repository
      Reservation -> Core: uow.commit() only on success
    else Expired, invalid owner/state/version or unavailable
      Reservation -> Reservation: Reject pickup; no Trip or pickup writes
      note right of Reservation
        Expiry / incident maintenance is a separate M2 operation.
        M2 releases its own claim and requests the permitted
        Core transition; Core does not run an expiry sweep.
      end note
    end
  end
  Reservation --> UI: Trip or error; reread M2 record after race conflict
end
UI --> Student: Pickup / due time or recovery guidance
note over Reservation,Core
  Explicit commit includes M2 and Core writes; otherwise rollback.
  The deadline is exclusive: pickup at expiry is rejected.
end note
@enduml
